  "beats": [
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "A Ukrainian kamikaze drone struck the Crimean Bridge, damaging the structure and prompting Russian authorities to close it to vehicle traffic.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-16:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:00:08Z",
      "text": "Ukrainian military intelligence said that on 10 November, one Russian Serna-class landing craft and one other craft were sunk by drone boats in Vuzka Bay, Crimea.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1386105508:127"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:00:15Z",
      "text": "Since July 2022, a series of explosions and fires has occurred on the Russian-occupied Crimean Peninsula, which the Russian Army used to launch its offensive on Southern Ukraine.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1386105508:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:00:25Z",
      "text": "The map shows Ukraine, where the reports place the events.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-16:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:00:33Z",
      "text": "According to the Russian claim recorded by Wikipedia, 3 rockets, 70+ aerial drones and 15+ maritime drones were shot down or destroyed.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1386105508:casualties-side-2-"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:00:38Z",
      "text": "As Wikipedia records, 9 civilians were killed and 126 were injured.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1386105508:casualties"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:00:44Z",
      "text": "IODA recorded responsive internet address blocks in Ukraine falling to 88% of their usual level on 2026-11-04.",
      "cites": [
        "ioda:UA:ping:day:2026-11-04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:00:49Z",
      "text": "By 2026-11-16, the same measure had recovered to 98% of its usual level.",
      "cites": [
        "ioda:UA:ping:day:2026-11-16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:00:56Z",
      "text": "Crimea is also named in the reports.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-16:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:01:05Z",
      "text": "The story has been reported by The Guardian and the BBC.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-16:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:01:13Z",
      "text": "France 24 headlined it: Live: 600 Ukrainian drones target Moscow, and the Crimea bridge strike halts traffic.",
      "cites": [
        "news:france24:59995b76c236"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:01:19Z",
      "text": "BBC News headlined it: Landmark Crimea bridge hit as Russia reports biggest Ukrainian drone attack of war.",
      "cites": [
        "news:bbc:b9b16089c989"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:01:25Z",
      "text": "The Guardian headlined it: Ukraine hits Kerch bridge between Russia and occupied Crimea.",
      "cites": [
        "news:guardian:3c35d058abb8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:01:34Z",
      "text": "Sources include Wikipedia current events and articles, Wikimedia pageviews, Wikidata, and IODA at Georgia Tech.",
